The site's second change to the scene of "White Room, Pixel Traced": a Monstera
deliciosa in a mid-century planter (a low ochre bowl on a chrome plinth),
applied by scripts/vendor-whiteroom.sh after scripts/whiteroom-scene.patch.

The plant is the scene's 8th group (the renderer takes up to 8), a little way
out from the back wall at the left of the room, where the site's wide frames
show it and the page's 3:2 frame does not. Its primitives come from ../monstera-scene.js, the
site's own code: new kinds (LEAF, CONE, CLUSTER) and materials (LEAF .. FURL),
which whiteroom.ts teaches the room's shader (monstera-shader.ts). The leaves'
codes (maturity, freshness, a torn margin) go out with the scene, for the leaf
maps the renderer bakes. The uplighter's cable used to stop on the open floor;
its last metre and a half now curves back to the wall and runs along the
cove at its foot, behind the planter, to a wall socket the pot hides.

